use /lib

export shape TaskTableStreamingShape:
    description:
        While the run is under way, the table ends in a waiting row for
        whatever the harness does next. As soon as a row's type is known, its
        badge is real, and as soon as its text or argument arrives, that is
        shown.

    rawOutput:
        Until a row has something meaningful to show, its Type cell is a
        skeleton and its Output cell shows the last three lines of the
        harness's raw JSON output: muted, monospace, JSON syntax-highlighted,
        and always three lines tall so the row doesn't jump. Before any output
        has arrived it reads "Waiting for the harness…".

    skeletons:
        While the input of a Files, Edit, Command, Web, or Agent call is still
        arriving, its Output cell shows only a skeleton.

        A skeleton stands in for a running row only while there is nothing
        meaningful to show for it. As soon as there is, no skeleton is shown for
        it at all.
